ent-MobAshWalker = ash walker
    .desc = A digitigrade reptilian native to Lavaland.
ent-AshWalkerEgg = ash walker egg
    .desc = A large yellow egg. A humanoid silhouette stirs beneath its shell.
ent-ClothingUniformAshWalker = ash walker uniform
    .desc = Simple tribal clothing, made for life among the ashes.
ghost-role-information-ash-walker-name = Ash Walker
ghost-role-information-ash-walker-description = You are a native of Lavaland. Hunt, feed the nest, and protect your tribe. You speak the reptilian language, do not need to breathe, and are immune to pressure and ash storms. Your scales reduce wounds, heat, cold, poison, and radiation damage. Lava and intense fire are still dangerous. You cannot use ordinary firearms or footwear.
ghost-role-information-ash-walker-rules = You are a [color=red][bold]Team Antagonist[/bold][/color]. Your tribe consists of the other ash walkers from your Lavaland. Support your kin and defend your settlement and its lands. Your relations with outsiders develop in play; destroying the station is not your objective. Do not use knowledge from a previous life.
ash-walker-cannot-equip-footwear = This footwear does not fit your digitigrade legs.
ash-walker-cannot-shoot = Your fingers do not fit this weapon's trigger mechanism.
ash-walker-clothing-cannot-equip = This equipment only fits ash walkers.
ash-walker-clothing-examine = Fitted to an ash walker's build. Other creatures cannot wear it.
ent-ClothingOuterArmorBoneAshWalker = ash walker bone armor
    .desc = Dense bone plates bound to fit an ash walker's powerful frame.
ent-ClothingHeadHelmetBoneAshWalker = ash walker bone helmet
    .desc = A reinforced skull helmet fitted for an ash walker's head.
ent-CrateAshWalkerHunting = ash walker hunting crate
    .desc = Bone armor, knives, bows and arrows for three hunters.
ent-CrateAshWalkerTools = ash walker workshop crate
    .desc = Mining and building tools, buckets, materials and spare light batteries for a small settlement.
ent-CrateAshWalkerSupplies = ash walker provisions crate
    .desc = Eighteen bottles of drinking water and twelve cooked steaks for the settlement's first hunts.
ent-CrateAshWalkerMedical = ash walker medical crate
    .desc = Bandages, ointment, trauma supplies, blood packs and emergency injectors for three hunters.
ent-AshWalkerNest = necropolis nest
    .desc = A living tendril that nurtures the tribe's eggs. It feeds on intact corpses offered by ash walkers. The ground nearby will collapse if the nest dies!
ent-AshWalkerEggIncubating = { ent-AshWalkerEgg }
    .desc = { ent-AshWalkerEgg.desc }
ent-AshWalkerNestCollapse = collapsing nest
    .desc = The dying tendril is pulling the ground down. Move away!
ent-AshWalkerWaterSource = stone spring
    .desc = An underground aquifer continuously fills this basin with clean water. Drink here or fill your bottles and buckets.
ash-walker-nest-sacrifice = Offer a sacrifice to the nest
ash-walker-nest-sacrifice-hint = Pull an intact corpse up to the nest. It accepts large Lavaland prey and humanoid bodies, except ash walkers. Small, summoned, legion-infested and butchered creatures are unsuitable. The nest must have room for the entire offering.
ash-walker-nest-consumed = The nest consumes { $body }, nourishing its eggs with fresh flesh!
ash-walker-nest-status = Flesh: [color=red]{ $flesh }/{ $capacity }[/color]. Egg cost: { $cost }. Tribal eggs: { $eggs }/{ $limit }.
ash-walker-nest-instructions = The nest accepts intact dead prey brought to its roots. The ritual requires stillness; injury interrupts the offering. The victim's equipment will remain on the ground. Immature eggs will die with the nest.
ash-walker-egg-incubating = Its shell is still soft. The egg draws strength from the nest and is not ready to hatch.
ash-walker-egg-matured = The shell hardens. The egg is ready to hatch!
ent-DaggerBone = bone dagger
    .desc = A sharpened bone with a comfortable grip, suited to skinning prey and cutting sinew.
ent-AxeBone = bone axe
    .desc = Heavy bone plates lashed to a sturdy haft. A two-handed grip gives its edge the weight to split timber and thick hides.
ent-SinewCuffs = sinew restraints
    .desc = Tough strands of watcher sinew tied into a pair of reusable restraints.
ent-ClothingHandsGlovesBoneBracers = bone bracers
    .desc = Overlapping bone plates tied around the forearms. They soften blows without covering the fingers.
ent-ClothingNeckBoneTalisman = bone talisman
    .desc = A hunter's charm carved from bone and bound with sinew. The old gods favor those who return from the hunt.
ent-ClothingUniformSkullArmor = skull-plated loincloth
    .desc = A hide loincloth reinforced with a carved skull plate to protect the groin.
ent-ClothingBeltAshWalker = hunter's belt
    .desc = Hide pouches sewn with watcher sinew. Keeps knives, provisions, bindings and small tools close at hand.
ent-ClothingOuterCloakGoliath = goliath hide cloak
    .desc = A thick cloak lined with a goliath's rocky plates. Its hide resists claws and heat, while the attached hood protects the head.
ent-ClothingHeadHoodGoliath = goliath hide hood
    .desc = A thick hide hood that shields the head from glancing blows and searing heat.
ent-BowBone = bone shortbow
    .desc = A composite bow made from curved bones and watcher sinew. Its limbs need both hands to draw.
ent-ArrowBone = bone arrow
    .desc = A slender bone shaft with a carved point and vanes. It can be recovered after a shot.
ash-walker-construction-spear-name = Bone spear with sinew
ash-walker-construction-spear-description = A bone spear bound with watcher sinew.
ent-BookAshWalkerRecipes = hunter's craft book
    .desc = A smoke-stained book bound in hide. Its drawings show how to turn a successful hunt into weapons and clothing.
ash-walker-recipe-book-content =
    [bold]CRAFT OF THE ASH CHILDREN[/bold]

    First decide who receives the prey: the nest or the hunters. The nest accepts only whole bodies. A butchered beast cannot become a second offering.

    [bold]What the hunt provides[/bold]
    Take a knife from the hunting crate and butcher a dead beast. A bone dagger can replace it later.
    Watcher: 1 bone and 2 sinews.
    Goliath: 2 bones, 2 to 4 pieces of hide and 2 cuts of meat.
    Legion: 2 bones; keep its other trophies separately.
    All sinew below means watcher sinew, and all hide means goliath hide. Count individual pieces, not bundles.

    [bold]Weapons[/bold]
    Bone dagger — 2 bones.
    Sinew-bound bone spear — 4 bones and 1 sinew.
    Bone axe — 6 bones and 3 sinews.
    Bone shortbow — 4 bones and 2 sinews.
    Bone arrow — 1 bone for each arrow.

    [bold]Armor and clothing[/bold]
    Ash walker bone armor — 6 bones.
    Ash walker bone helmet — 4 bones.
    Bone bracers — 2 bones and 1 sinew.
    Bone talisman — 2 bones and 1 sinew.
    Skull-plated loincloth — 2 bones and 1 hide.
    Goliath hide cloak with hood — 2 hides and 2 sinews.

    [bold]Equipment[/bold]
    Sinew restraints — 1 sinew.
    Hunter's belt — 1 hide and 2 sinews.

    [bold]A craft master's advice[/bold]
    These armors are fitted to an ash walker's body. Outsiders cannot wear them.
    A tribal hunter knows the weak spots of local beasts and deals half again as much weapon damage to them.
    Keep the materials close: none of these crafts requires a workbench.
    The dagger speeds up butchering. Hold the axe with both hands for a heavy blow; it also chops logs.
    The bow needs both hands. Surviving bone arrows can be recovered and fired again.
    The cloak takes the place of outer armor. Remove your helmet before raising its hood. Hide softens heat and blows, but will not save you from a swim in lava.
    Fill the belt with knives, arrows, bandages, food, bindings, materials and small tools. Carry the heavy axe on your back or on the outside of your cloak.
